module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Flatness.FinitePresentationStalk05I7
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Flat.DevissageLocalize

/-!
# Localizing the prime data of a complete dévissage at the base prime

`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Flat.DevissageLocalize` base changes a complete dévissage of `N/S/R` over
a prime `r` of `R` to the local ring `R_r`, as `Module.CompleteDevissage.localizeAtPrime`. That
transports the dévissage itself and none of the prime data: the nine stage-prime conditions which
`Module.CompleteDevissage.PrimeData` packages, and which
`Module.CompleteDevissage.finitePresentation_of_flat` consumes, are a separate structure over the
dévissage and have to be carried across separately. This file carries them across:
`Module.CompleteDevissage.PrimeData.localize` turns a `D.PrimeData q` into a
`D.localizeAtPrime.PrimeData (qS_r)`.

Every field is a prime correspondence for a localization. The localized stage primes are the
images `pᵢS_r` of the original ones, and the whole transport rests on two facts about a
localization `C → C_P` and a prime `p` of `C` missing the inverted set: `pC_P` is again prime with
`p` as its contraction (`IsLocalization.isPrime_of_isPrime_disjoint` and
`IsLocalization.under_map_of_isPrime_disjoint`), and contraction is injective on *all* ideals of
`C_P` (`IsLocalization.map_under`). The inverted set misses every stage prime for one reason:
each stage prime contracts to `r` in the base, so it cannot contain the image of an element
outside `r`.

## Main definitions

* `Module.CompleteDevissage.PrimeData.localize`: the base change of the prime data of a complete
  dévissage to the local ring at the base prime, over
  `Module.CompleteDevissage.localizeAtPrime`.
* `Module.CompleteDevissage.PrimeData.locLowerPrime` and
  `Module.CompleteDevissage.PrimeData.locUpperPrime`: the localized stage primes, the two data
  fields of the result.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Flatness.eq_of_comap_algebraMap_eq`: two ideals of a localization with the same
  contraction are equal. This is the uniqueness principle every field is proved by: the localized
  primes are pinned down by their contractions, which the original prime data computes.
* `Stacks.Flatness.disjoint_algebraMapSubmonoid_of_comap_eq`: a prime contracting to `r` misses
  the image of the complement of `r`. This is the disjointness hypothesis of every localization
  prime-correspondence lemma used here, and it is why no stage prime has to be assumed to survive
  the localization.
* `Stacks.Flatness.comap_map_eq_map_of_comap_eq`: contraction along a localized ring map takes the
  image of a prime to the image of its contraction. This is `upperPrime_under`, `initial_under`
  and `transition_under` at once, since the three differ only in which map of the dévissage is
  localized.
* `Module.CompleteDevissage.PrimeData.isPrime`: the prime of `S` carried by prime data is prime.
  It is the contraction of the first upper prime, so this needs no hypothesis — which is why
  `Module.CompleteDevissage.PrimeData.localize` assumes no primality of `q`.
* `Module.CompleteDevissage.PrimeData.upperPrime_comap_algebraMap`: each upper stage prime
  contracts to the prime of the base, which `Module.CompleteDevissage.PrimeData` records only for
  the lower primes.

## Implementation notes

The fields of the result are assigned whole functions, `lowerPrime := pd.locLowerPrime` rather
than `lowerPrime i := …`, as in `Module.CompleteDevissage.localize`. The reason is that the stage
index of the localized dévissage has type `Fin (D.localizeAtPrime.stepCount + 1)`, which is
definitionally but not reducibly `Fin (D.stepCount + 1)`, so a field written stage by stage puts
`D.B i` and `D.A i` out of reach of instance search. Assigning a function defers the conversion
to a single definitional-unfolding check on the function type, where no instance has to be
synthesized.

For the same reason the nine conditions are proved as separate lemmas indexed by
`i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)` and stated in terms of `Module.CompleteDevissage.locA`,
`locB`, `locToLeft`, `locToRight` and `locToA₀`, rather than in terms of the projections of
`Module.CompleteDevissage.localizeAtPrime`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05HX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05HX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05I1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05I1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05I4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05I4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05I5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05I5)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

namespace Stacks.Flatness

/-- **Contraction is injective on the ideals of a localization.** Two ideals of `C_P` with the
same contraction to `C` are equal, because every ideal of `C_P` is generated by its contraction
(`IsLocalization.map_under`).

No primality is needed, and this is the form in which the localized stage primes are identified:
each is pinned down by its contraction, which the original prime data computes. -/
theorem eq_of_comap_algebraMap_eq {C C' : Type*} [CommRing C] [CommRing C'] [Algebra C C']
    (P : Submonoid C) [IsLocalization P C'] {I J : Ideal C'}
    (h : I.comap (algebraMap C C') = J.comap (algebraMap C C')) : I = J := by
  rw [← IsLocalization.map_under P C' I, ← IsLocalization.map_under P C' J]
  exact congrArg _ h

/-- **A prime contracting to `r` misses the image of the complement of `r`.**

This is the disjointness hypothesis of every localization prime-correspondence used in the
transport of prime data, and it is the reason no stage prime has to be assumed to survive the
localization: `Module.CompleteDevissage.PrimeData` already records that each lower stage prime
contracts to `r`, and `Module.CompleteDevissage.PrimeData.upperPrime_comap_algebraMap` derives
the same for the upper ones. -/
theorem disjoint_algebraMapSubmonoid_of_comap_eq {R C : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing C]
    [Algebra R C] {r : Ideal R} [r.IsPrime] {p : Ideal C}
    (hp : p.comap (algebraMap R C) = r) :
    Disjoint ((Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid C r.primeCompl : Submonoid C) : Set C) (p : Set C) := by
  rw [Set.disjoint_left]
  rintro x ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩ hx
  exact ha (hp ▸ hx)

/-- **Contraction along a localized ring map takes the image of a prime to the image of its
contraction.**

Let `φ : B → A` be a ring map and let `φ' : B' → A'` be a map of localizations over it, meaning
`hφ`. If `P` is a prime of `A` with contraction `pb` along `φ`, and the inverted sets miss `P`
and `pb` respectively, then `PA'` contracts along `φ'` to `pbB'`.

Both sides are identified by their contractions to `B` using
`Stacks.Flatness.eq_of_comap_algebraMap_eq`: `hφ` turns the contraction of `PA'` along
`φ'` then `B → B'` into its contraction along `φ` then `A → A'`, and
`IsLocalization.under_map_of_isPrime_disjoint` discharges both localizations.

This single lemma is `upperPrime_under`, `initial_under` and `transition_under` of
`Module.CompleteDevissage.PrimeData.localize`, which differ only in which map of the dévissage is
being localized. -/
theorem comap_map_eq_map_of_comap_eq {B A B' A' : Type*} [CommRing B] [CommRing A] [CommRing B']
    [CommRing A'] [Algebra B B'] [Algebra A A'] (T : Submonoid B) [IsLocalization T B']
    (U : Submonoid A) [IsLocalization U A'] (φ : B →+* A) (φ' : B' →+* A')
    (hφ : ∀ b, φ' (algebraMap B B' b) = algebraMap A A' (φ b)) (P : Ideal A) (hP : P.IsPrime)
    (pb : Ideal B) (hpb : P.comap φ = pb) (hU : Disjoint (U : Set A) (P : Set A))
    (hT : Disjoint (T : Set B) (pb : Set B)) :
    (Ideal.map (algebraMap A A') P).comap φ' = Ideal.map (algebraMap B B') pb := by
  subst hpb
  have := hP
  refine eq_of_comap_algebraMap_eq T ?_
  have hcomp : φ'.comp (algebraMap B B') = (algebraMap A A').comp φ := RingHom.ext hφ
  have hA : (Ideal.map (algebraMap A A') P).comap (algebraMap A A') = P :=
    IsLocalization.under_map_of_isPrime_disjoint U A' hP hU
  have hB : (Ideal.map (algebraMap B B') (P.comap φ)).comap (algebraMap B B') = P.comap φ :=
    IsLocalization.under_map_of_isPrime_disjoint T B' (Ideal.IsPrime.comap φ) hT
  rw [Ideal.comap_comap, hcomp, ← Ideal.comap_comap, hA, hB]

end Stacks.Flatness

namespace Module.CompleteDevissage.PrimeData

variable {R S N : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] [Algebra.FiniteType R S]
  [AddCommGroup N] [Module S N] [Module.Finite S N] {r : Ideal R} [r.IsPrime]
  {D : CompleteDevissage R S N r} {q : Ideal S} (pd : D.PrimeData q)

/-! ### Consequences of the prime data in the original dévissage -/

/-- **Each upper stage prime contracts to the prime of the base.**
`Module.CompleteDevissage.PrimeData` records this for the lower primes only; for the upper ones it
follows by contracting through the lower prime along `toLeft i`, which is a map of
`R`-algebras. -/
theorem upperPrime_comap_algebraMap (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) :
    (pd.upperPrime i).comap (algebraMap R (D.A i)) = r := by
  rw [← show (D.toLeft i).toRingHom.comp (algebraMap R (D.B i)) = algebraMap R (D.A i) from
      (D.toLeft i).comp_algebraMap, ← Ideal.comap_comap, pd.upperPrime_under i,
    pd.lowerPrime_under i]

include pd in
/-- **The prime of `S` carried by prime data is prime.** It is the contraction of the first upper
prime, which is prime, so this is not an extra hypothesis — unlike in
`Module.CompleteDevissage.finitePresentation_of_flat`, where `q.IsPrime` is assumed. -/
theorem isPrime : q.IsPrime := by
  have := pd.upperPrime_isPrime 0
  rw [← pd.initial_under]
  exact Ideal.IsPrime.comap D.toA₀.toRingHom

/-! ### The localized stage primes -/

/-- The localized lower stage prime: the ideal generated in the localized lower algebra by the
lower stage prime of the original prime data. -/
noncomputable def locLowerPrime (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) : Ideal (D.locB i) :=
  Ideal.map (algebraMap (D.B i) (D.locB i)) (pd.lowerPrime i)

/-- The localized upper stage prime: the ideal generated in the localized upper algebra by the
upper stage prime of the original prime data. -/
noncomputable def locUpperPrime (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) : Ideal (D.locA i) :=
  Ideal.map (algebraMap (D.A i) (D.locA i)) (pd.upperPrime i)

/-- The localized lower stage prime is the image of the original one. -/
theorem locLowerPrime_def (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) :
    pd.locLowerPrime i = Ideal.map (algebraMap (D.B i) (D.locB i)) (pd.lowerPrime i) := rfl

/-- The localized upper stage prime is the image of the original one. -/
theorem locUpperPrime_def (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) :
    pd.locUpperPrime i = Ideal.map (algebraMap (D.A i) (D.locA i)) (pd.upperPrime i) := rfl

/-- The original lower stage prime is the contraction of the localized one, since the inverted
set misses it. -/
theorem comap_locLowerPrime (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) :
    (pd.locLowerPrime i).comap (algebraMap (D.B i) (D.locB i)) = pd.lowerPrime i :=
  IsLocalization.under_map_of_isPrime_disjoint
    (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (D.B i) r.primeCompl) (D.locB i) (pd.lowerPrime_isPrime i)
    (Stacks.Flatness.disjoint_algebraMapSubmonoid_of_comap_eq (pd.lowerPrime_under i))

/-- **The localized lower stage prime is prime.** The inverted set misses the original lower
prime, because that prime contracts to `r`. -/
theorem locLowerPrime_isPrime (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) : (pd.locLowerPrime i).IsPrime :=
  IsLocalization.isPrime_of_isPrime_disjoint
    (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (D.B i) r.primeCompl) (D.locB i) _ (pd.lowerPrime_isPrime i)
    (Stacks.Flatness.disjoint_algebraMapSubmonoid_of_comap_eq (pd.lowerPrime_under i))

/-- **The localized upper stage prime is prime.** The inverted set misses the original upper
prime, because that prime contracts to `r` by
`Module.CompleteDevissage.PrimeData.upperPrime_comap_algebraMap`. -/
theorem locUpperPrime_isPrime (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) : (pd.locUpperPrime i).IsPrime :=
  IsLocalization.isPrime_of_isPrime_disjoint
    (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (D.A i) r.primeCompl) (D.locA i) _ (pd.upperPrime_isPrime i)
    (Stacks.Flatness.disjoint_algebraMapSubmonoid_of_comap_eq
      (pd.upperPrime_comap_algebraMap i))

/-- **The localized lower stage prime contracts to the prime of the localized base.**

Both sides are ideals of the localized base `R_r`, so by
`Stacks.Flatness.eq_of_comap_algebraMap_eq` it is enough to contract them to `R`. The left side
contracts through `Bᵢ`, where the original lower prime reappears and contracts to `r`; the right
side is `rR_r`, whose contraction is `r` because `r` misses its own complement. -/
theorem locLowerPrime_under (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) :
    (pd.locLowerPrime i).comap (algebraMap (Localization r.primeCompl) (D.locB i))
      = Ideal.map (algebraMap R (Localization r.primeCompl)) r := by
  refine Stacks.Flatness.eq_of_comap_algebraMap_eq r.primeCompl ?_
  have hR : (Ideal.map (algebraMap R (Localization r.primeCompl)) r).comap
      (algebraMap R (Localization r.primeCompl)) = r :=
    IsLocalization.under_map_of_isPrime_disjoint r.primeCompl (Localization r.primeCompl) ‹_›
      (Set.disjoint_left.mpr fun _ hx hx' => hx hx')
  rw [Ideal.comap_comap, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq R (Localization r.primeCompl) (D.locB i),
    IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq R (D.B i) (D.locB i), ← Ideal.comap_comap,
    pd.comap_locLowerPrime i, pd.lowerPrime_under i, hR]

/-! ### The localized conditions -/

/-- **The localized upper stage prime contracts to the localized lower stage prime.** This is
`Stacks.Flatness.comap_map_eq_map_of_comap_eq` for the localization of `toLeft i`, whose
compatibility with the localization maps is
`Module.CompleteDevissage.locToLeft_algebraMap`. -/
theorem locUpperPrime_under (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) :
    (pd.locUpperPrime i).comap (D.locToLeft i).toRingHom = pd.locLowerPrime i :=
  Stacks.Flatness.comap_map_eq_map_of_comap_eq
    (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (D.B i) r.primeCompl)
    (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (D.A i) r.primeCompl) (D.toLeft i).toRingHom
    (D.locToLeft i).toRingHom (D.locToLeft_algebraMap i) _ (pd.upperPrime_isPrime i) _
    (pd.upperPrime_under i)
    (Stacks.Flatness.disjoint_algebraMapSubmonoid_of_comap_eq (pd.upperPrime_comap_algebraMap i))
    (Stacks.Flatness.disjoint_algebraMapSubmonoid_of_comap_eq (pd.lowerPrime_under i))

/-- **The localized upper stage prime is the unique prime above the localized lower one.**

A prime `p` of the localized upper algebra contracting to the localized lower prime contracts,
through `Aᵢ`, to a prime of `Aᵢ` above the original lower prime; by
`Module.CompleteDevissage.PrimeData.upperPrime_unique` that contraction is the original upper
prime, and `p` is generated by its own contraction (`IsLocalization.map_under`). -/
theorem locUpperPrime_unique (i : Fin (D.stepCount + 1)) (p : Ideal (D.locA i)) (hp : p.IsPrime)
    (h : p.comap (D.locToLeft i).toRingHom = pd.locLowerPrime i) : p = pd.locUpperPrime i := by
  have := hp
  have key : (p.comap (algebraMap (D.A i) (D.locA i))).comap (D.toLeft i).toRingHom
      = pd.lowerPrime i := by
    rw [Ideal.comap_comap,
      show (algebraMap (D.A i) (D.locA i)).comp (D.toLeft i).toRingHom
          = (D.locToLeft i).toRingHom.comp (algebraMap (D.B i) (D.locB i)) from
        RingHom.ext fun b => (D.locToLeft_algebraMap i b).symm,
      ← Ideal.comap_comap, h, pd.comap_locLowerPrime i]
  have hmap : Ideal.map (algebraMap (D.A i) (D.locA i))
      (p.comap (algebraMap (D.A i) (D.locA i))) = p :=
    IsLocalization.map_under (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (D.A i) r.primeCompl) (D.locA i) p
  rw [pd.locUpperPrime_def i,
    ← pd.upperPrime_unique i _ (Ideal.IsPrime.comap (algebraMap (D.A i) (D.locA i))) key, hmap]

/-- **The localized prime of the algebra is the contraction of the first localized upper prime.**
This is `Stacks.Flatness.comap_map_eq_map_of_comap_eq` for the localization of `toA₀`, whose
compatibility with the localization maps is `Module.CompleteDevissage.locToA₀_algebraMap`. The
inverted set misses `q` because `q` contracts to `r`, which is
`Module.CompleteDevissage.PrimeData.under_eq`. -/
theorem locInitial_under :
    (pd.locUpperPrime 0).comap
        (D.locToA₀ (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid S r.primeCompl))).toRingHom
      = Ideal.map (algebraMap S (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid S r.primeCompl))) q :=
  Stacks.Flatness.comap_map_eq_map_of_comap_eq (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid S r.primeCompl)
    (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (D.A 0) r.primeCompl) D.toA₀.toRingHom
    (D.locToA₀ (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid S r.primeCompl))).toRingHom
    (D.locToA₀_algebraMap (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid S r.primeCompl))) _
    (pd.upperPrime_isPrime 0) _ pd.initial_under
    (Stacks.Flatness.disjoint_algebraMapSubmonoid_of_comap_eq
      (pd.upperPrime_comap_algebraMap 0))
    (Stacks.Flatness.disjoint_algebraMapSubmonoid_of_comap_eq pd.under_eq)

/-- **Consecutive localized stages carry compatible primes.** This is
`Stacks.Flatness.comap_map_eq_map_of_comap_eq` for the localization of `toRight i`, whose
compatibility with the localization maps is
`Module.CompleteDevissage.locToRight_algebraMap`. -/
theorem locTransition_under (i : Fin D.stepCount) :
    (pd.locUpperPrime i.succ).comap (D.locToRight i).toRingHom
      = pd.locLowerPrime i.castSucc :=
  Stacks.Flatness.comap_map_eq_map_of_comap_eq
    (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (D.B i.castSucc) r.primeCompl)
    (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (D.A i.succ) r.primeCompl) (D.toRight i).toRingHom
    (D.locToRight i).toRingHom (D.locToRight_algebraMap i) _ (pd.upperPrime_isPrime i.succ) _
    (pd.transition_under i)
    (Stacks.Flatness.disjoint_algebraMapSubmonoid_of_comap_eq
      (pd.upperPrime_comap_algebraMap i.succ))
    (Stacks.Flatness.disjoint_algebraMapSubmonoid_of_comap_eq
      (pd.lowerPrime_under i.castSucc))

/-! ### The transported prime data -/

/-- **The base change of the prime data of a complete dévissage to the local ring at the base
prime.**

Given a complete dévissage `D` of `N/S/R` over a prime `r` of `R` together with prime data over a
prime `q` of `S` (Stacks 05HX and the nine conditions of
`Module.CompleteDevissage.PrimeData`), the localized dévissage
`Module.CompleteDevissage.localizeAtPrime` carries prime data over the localized prime `qS_r`,
with the images of the original stage primes as its stage primes.

This is the transport the localization step of Stacks 05I1 needs:
`Module.CompleteDevissage.localizeAtPrime` carries the dévissage to the local ring of the base,
and this carries the prime data that
`Module.CompleteDevissage.finitePresentation_of_flat` consumes alongside it, so that a dévissage
with prime data produced before localizing yields one after.

No primality of `q` is assumed: it follows from the prime data by
`Module.CompleteDevissage.PrimeData.isPrime`. -/
noncomputable def localize :
    D.localizeAtPrime.PrimeData
      (Ideal.map (algebraMap S (Localization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid S r.primeCompl))) q)
    where
  lowerPrime := pd.locLowerPrime
  lowerPrime_isPrime := pd.locLowerPrime_isPrime
  lowerPrime_under := pd.locLowerPrime_under
  upperPrime := pd.locUpperPrime
  upperPrime_isPrime := pd.locUpperPrime_isPrime
  upperPrime_under := pd.locUpperPrime_under
  upperPrime_unique := pd.locUpperPrime_unique
  initial_under := pd.locInitial_under
  transition_under := pd.locTransition_under

end Module.CompleteDevissage.PrimeData

end
